---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import GroveGantry from '../components/GroveGantry.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import { GROVE_PARTS } from '../data/grove';

const updated = new Date('2026-09-19');
const updatedLabel = updated.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
const version = 'v1.1.18';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Grove — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Grove (gw): one feature branch across several repositories, drawn as a gantry riding parallel rails. Create, inspect, sync and remove a workspace as one unit."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<header class="intro">
				<div class="meta"><h1>Grove</h1><time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{updatedLabel}</time></div>
				<p class="lede">
					A CLI I wrote for working across several repos at once, drawn as a gantry: each repo is a rail, the
					workspace is the carriage that rides all of them together. Scroll to run it. Code on
					<a href="https://github.com/nicksenap/grove" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>, docs in the
					<a href="https://github.com/nicksenap/grove#documentation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">README</a>.
				</p>
			</header>

			<GroveGantry />

			<section class="bom" aria-labelledby="parts-title">
				<h2 id="parts-title">Parts</h2>
				<ol class="parts">
					{GROVE_PARTS.map((p, i) => (
						<li class="part" id={`part-${p.id}`}>
							<span class="idx">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
							<div class="body">
								<div class="head">
									<span class="name">{p.name}</span>
									<span class="slot">{p.role} · the {p.part}</span>
								</div>
								<p class="blurb">{p.blurb}</p>
							</div>
						</li>
					))}
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="why-title">
				<h2 id="why-title">Why</h2>
				<p>
					Monorepos get cross-project work for free. Most of what I touch is not a monorepo: separate repos,
					separate CI, separate deploys. A feature across a web app, an API and a worker meant
					<code>git worktree add</code> three times, three branch names to keep aligned, three places to check
					and three to clean up. Grove is that set of chores collapsed into one carriage, without moving
					anything into a monorepo.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="install-title">
				<h2 id="install-title">Install</h2>
				<p>A single static binary; git is the only thing it needs on PATH.</p>
				<pre><code><span class="comment"># macOS / Linux</span>
brew install nicksenap/grove/grove

<span class="comment"># lets gw go / gw create change directory; add to .zshrc or .bashrc</span>
eval "$(gw shell-init)"

<span class="comment"># register the directory that holds your repos, then make a workspace</span>
gw init ~/dev
gw create -b feat/login -r web,api,worker
gw status feat-login</code></pre>
			</section>

			<p class="colophon">
				<em>grove</em>, noun: a small group of trees growing together. Drawn in code with
				<a href="https://zzz.dog" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Zdog</a>, as a three-rail linear gantry. Started in Python,
				<a href="/thoughts/rewriting-grove-in-go">rewritten in Go</a> for startup time and a one-file install. This
				page describes {version}; the date above is the last time it matched the tool.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.intro {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.meta {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 1ch;
	}
	.meta time {
		color: var(--dim);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.lede {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 60ch;
	}
	section {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
	section > p {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}
	.parts {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		box-shadow: var(--fg) 0 1px 0 0 inset;
	}
	.part {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 3ch 1fr;
		gap: 0 1ch;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		box-shadow: var(--border) 0 -1px 0 0 inset;
	}
	.idx {
		color: var(--dim);
	}
	.head {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0 1.5ch;
		align-items: baseline;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}
	.name {
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.slot {
		color: var(--dim);
	}
	.blurb {
		margin: 0;
		opacity: 0.75;
		max-width: 62ch;
	}
	pre {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.comment {
		color: var(--dim);
	}
	.colophon {
		margin: 2rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		opacity: 0.5;
	}
</style>
